The “state minimum standard codes” as defined as O.C.G.A. § 8-2-20(9)(b)@) as the same may hereinafter be amended or revised, are hereby adopted in their entirety by the Town of Sharpsburg, and are made a part hereof as fully as through stated verbatim herein, to wit:

- (1) International Building Code;

- (2) National Electrical Code (NFPA);

- (3) International Fuel Gas Code;

- (4) International Mechanical Code;

- (5) International Plumbing Code;

- (6) International Residential Code for One-and-Two Family Dwellings;

- (7) International Energy Conservation Code; and

- (8) International Fire Code;_and

- (9) International Property Maintenance Code.

The Department of Community Affairs Board specifically omitted the plumbing and electrical requirements of the International Residential code for One-and-Two Family Dwellings. Therefore, the plumbing requirements of the International Plumbing Code and the electrical requirements of the National Electrical Code must be used for one and two-family dwelling constructions.
